# Definition of Done Gate Rule

Use this as a hard governance gate for all projects and modules.

## DONE is allowed only when all conditions are true
1) Scope closure:
- 100% committed in-scope work items are `DONE`.
- No remaining `TODO`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `BLOCKED`, `READY_FOR_*` in committed scope.

2) Quality and security closure:
- Required build/test checks pass.
- Security gate passes with no unresolved critical/high issues (or approved waiver record).
- Business correctness, performance, and UI/UX acceptance evidence are attached.

3) Delivery governance closure:
- Required QA and QC gate decision is `GO` (or `GO WITH CONDITIONS` with all conditions closed).
- Required PM/SA/BA/QA/QC signoffs are recorded.

4) Evidence closure:
- Evidence paths are present and reproducible.
- Traceability is complete from requirement -> implementation -> test.

## Forced status mapping
- If any condition above is false, status must be `NOT DONE` (or `PARTIAL/IN DELIVERY`).
- Claiming `DONE` while conditions are open is non-compliant.

## Exception policy
- Any temporary exception requires:
  - explicit owner
  - rationale
  - expiry date
  - mitigation and follow-up task
